WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.410
Leah: If a child or young person
suffers any risk factors or starts

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.740
to show signs of distress, families,
communities and schools should support

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.350
them to cope better with the challenges
that life throws at them and try to be

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.030
there to listen to them when needed.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.810
Rhiannon: Schools can often play a
critical role in giving young people

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:22.360
the skills they need to form strong
interpersonal relationships, which

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.280
will support resilience such as
buddy systems, peer to peer support

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.820
networks, and anti-bullying initiatives.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.650
Leah: Schools that promote strong
social relationships and teach

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.760
practical coping skills, are likely
to have more resilient pupils, who

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.479
are able to learn more effectively.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:43.150
Schools as well as families and friends
can help young people to learn how to

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:47.609
regulate their emotions, solve problems
and help them plan things that might help

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.490
them cope better when life gets tough.

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:54.240
Rhiannon: A child or young person can
help themselves, by keeping a diary to

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.450
aid focus on more positive memories.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.070
They can also keep busy doing
things they enjoy, such as sports,

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.700
music or drama, and try and stay
away from the sources of stress.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.820
Once the risk factors have been recognised
and understood by all concerned, they can

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.839
then be addressed, and the child or young
person can be better supported to maintain

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.339
good mental health and well-being.

